Third-party methodologies, frameworks & trademarks
---------------------------------------------------

AOS is an original synthesis — the 7+1 Layer Framework and the AOS skill set are
the authors' own work. Where AOS applies established third-party methodologies,
credit is given here:

- Jobs-to-be-Done (JTBD) — the term was coined by Anthony (Tony) W. Ulwick
  (Strategyn) in 1990; the "Jobs Theory" framing was popularised by the late
  Clayton M. Christensen. AOS uses "Jobs-to-be-Done" / "JTBD" as a generic
  methodology term — no active trademark covers it (a 2015 application was
  abandoned). AOS does not use, and does not imply endorsement of, Strategyn's
  Outcome-Driven Innovation process.

- The Hero's Journey (the monomyth) — Joseph Campbell, "The Hero with a Thousand
  Faces" (1949). Used as one storytelling-framework option in the
  content-framework library.

- Before-After-Bridge — a classic direct-response copywriting formula in
  long-standing common use, with no single attributable author. Used as a
  storytelling-framework option.

- Stages of Awareness ("the awareness ladder") — Eugene M. Schwartz,
  "Breakthrough Advertising" (1966). Informs the ICP buying-stage model.

